  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "We now have both unimodal baselines: RNA-only (pca_n2000, singleprofile) at 48.5% accuracy and image-only (resnet50, singleprofile) at 20.8%. The most critical question for this multimodal study is whether combining these two modalities yields any benefit over the stronger unimodal baseline. config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000 + resnet50, concat) uses the exact same encoders as both completed experiments, making it a clean, single-variable test of fusion. If it exceeds 48.5%, multimodal is a promising direction and we should explore aggregation and better encoders; if it falls below, the weak image signal (20.8%) is likely to hurt rather than help, redirecting effort toward improving the image encoder or RNA multiprofile design. This experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the central design decision (unimodal vs. multimodal) before spending budget on more complex configurations."
}

